=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough Crystals to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise the Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the Gate Guard.
* Talk to {n:Apururu} in {z:Windurst Woods} HP #1 inside the northern **Manustery** building for a cutscene. You will obtain the {@k} {k:Manustery ring}.
* Talk to the following NPCs, in any order, to receive the {@k} {k:Rhinostery ring}, {@k} {k:Aurastery ring}, and {@k} {k:Optistery ring}:
** {n:Rukususu} in {z:Fei'Yin} at (F-6) on Map #2. Click the **Cermet Door** of the north-western small room for a cutscene with her.
*** {p:Home Point} #2 to {z:Fei'Yin} is the fastest way.
** {n:Sedal-Godjal} in {z:Davoi} (J-8). He can only be reached by going through {z:Monastic Cavern}. Enter {z:Monastic Cavern} from entrance 2 at (H-11) in {z:Davoi}. Once you're in, hug the right wall and exit at (H/I-8). Once you're back in {z:Davoi}, you can reach {n:Sedal-Godjal} by going east.
*** {p:Proto-Waypoint|Waypoint} to {z:Davoi} is the fastest way. Drop into the water, follow the water south-east to (J-10) to get back on land, then hug left until you reach entrance 2.
*** {p:Survival Guide} to {z:Davoi} is almost as fast.
** {n:Tosuka-Porika} in {z:Windurst Waters} North HP #1, inside the eastern **Optistery** building.
* Return to {n:Apururu} for dialogue regarding the final ring.

----
!Inner Horutoto Ruins-map4.jpg|right|Inner Horutoto Ruins Map 4
* Talk to {n:Kupipi} in {z:Heavens Tower} for a cutscene.
* Go to the tower in {z:West Sarutabaruta} (F-4) and enter {z:Outer Horutoto Ruins}.
** {z:Outer Horutoto Ruins} {p:Voidwatch} warp or {z:West Sarutabaruta}'s {p:Geomagnetic Fount|Waypoint} puts you right in front of this tower.
** Warping to the outpost/{p:Survival Guide} for {z:West Sarutabaruta} or warping to {z:Giddeus} and using {s:Escape} are the next best options.
* Go through the **Cracked Wall** at (I-6).
* Find the **Cracked Wall** at (G-8) on the second map. Touch it and pop {m:Queen of Coins|Queen of Coins (Monster)} (RDM) and {m:Queen of Swords|Queen of Swords (Monster)} (PLD).
* Click the **Cracked Wall** again (multiple times if needed) after defeating them for a cutscene and to obtain the {@k} {k:Orastery ring}.
* Return to {n:Apururu} for a cutscene.
* Talk to {p:Shantotto} in {z:Windurst Walls} at (K-7) for a cutscene and to obtain the {@k} {k:Glove of perpetual twilight}.
** You may need to speak to {p:Shantotto} multiple times for the correct cutscene.
* Return to {n:Apururu} for a cutscene.
* Go to {z:Inner Horutoto Ruins} and examine the **Gate of Darkness** at (I-7, south-eastern door) on Map 4 for a cutscene.
** Fastest way is using the {z:Toraimarai Canal} {p:Survival Guide} and then back tracking to Horutoto ruins.
** Alternatively, travel though {z:Toraimarai Canal} using the **Priming Gate** in {z:Windurst Walls} (H-3).
** You need to pass through the {p:Three Mage Gate} if you do not enter via the {z:Toraimarai Canal}.
* Return to {n:Apururu} for a cutscene that completes the Mission.
** (**Optional**) Return to {p:Shantotto} for dialogue regarding the {@k} {k:Glove of perpetual twilight}.
*** Ohohohoho! It looks like my glove of perpetual twilight had the desired effect! Ajido-Marujido's failure to regain consciousness is the only slight complication I was able to detect... But you don't need to go and start worrying. Why, it would take more than that to finish of a mage that had survived my tutelage and training! ...Now, about the glove of perpetual twilight. Due to a slight miscalculation on my part, the rings have become fused to the glove, I see. But don't worry. With a few twists, I'll soon have them free. I'll just hold on to the ministry rings for a little while longer. Ohohoho!
** (**Optional**) Return to {n:Tosuka-Porika} to report about the Book of the Gods as promised.
*** Where have you been? Did Ajido-Marujido get the book open!? ...Hrmm, he's fallen into a coma, has he...? He must've been drawn into the "World of the Book." If he manages to return to consciousness, he will have all the knowledge contained within the Book of the Gods. ...If he makes it back, that is.

